course: dictionary
lesson: 14962
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word reload is one of them. Re- means again, and load means to put something in or on, so reload often means to load something again.
explain: «The web page was stuck, so Sam hit reload.» Stuck is the clue. Sam wants the page to show its newest version, so in computing, reload means to open a page again. This meaning is also called refresh.
explain: «I need to reload my travel card before I get on the bus.» Here the clue is card. You cannot load a card with paper, but you can put more money on it again. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Reload can be a verb (to reload) or a noun (a reload).
fact: «Reload» means to load something again, such as a gun, a lorry or a dishwasher.
fact: In computing, «reload the page» means open it again so that it shows the newest version.
fact: «Reload a card» means to put more money or credit on it again.
fact: When a word has several meanings, look at the words around it to choose the right one.
exercise: «The web page was stuck, so Sam hit reload.» What does reload mean here? | Close the window for ever | Make the page bigger | *Open the page again to show the newest version | Print the page on paper
exercise: «I need to reload my travel card before the bus.» What does reload mean here? | Take the card apart | *Put more money on the card again | Draw a picture on the card | Throw the card away
exercise: «Dad had to reload the dishwasher after lunch.» What does reload mean? | Wash the dishwasher with cold water | *Load it again | Read its instructions out loud | Switch the dishwasher off for good
test: «Each reload took only a few seconds.» In this sentence, what kind of word is reload? | Verb | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb
test: «Sam hit reload and the news page changed.» What did reload do? | Closed the page for ever | Read the news out loud | *Opened the page again to show new news | Printed the news on paper
exam: «The printer ran out of paper, so Ella had to reload it.» What does reload mean here? | Load paper into it again | Make the printer louder | *Load paper into it again, as in refilling a printer | Stop the printer for ever
